V	set-version-ceiling	active	scripts/set-version-ceiling.sh	project|show|minor|major|no-minor|no-major|dry-run|help	yes	idempotent	POST	/operations/set-version-ceiling	SetVersionCeilingBody	action	DualChannelShellEnvelope	module:pgai_agent_kanban.ops.write.set_version_ceiling
V	switch-provider	active	scripts/switch-provider.sh	provider|help	yes	idempotent	POST	/operations/switch-provider	SwitchProviderBody	action	DualChannelShellEnvelope	module:pgai_agent_kanban.ops.write.switch_provider
# create-project's idempotence column reads "non-idempotent", corrected
# from an inherited "idempotent" default: the script's own regression test
# (team/tests/integration/test_create_project.py::
# test_create_project_refuses_duplicate_project_directory) locks in a
# non-zero exit when the target directory already exists, which is the
# exact state a same-arguments re-run produces -- a deliberate,
# already-shipped safety contract, not a bug to fix. Per this column's own
# header above ("treat a mismatch there as the correction, not this
# column"), the metadata is corrected to match the verified behaviour.
V	create-project	active	scripts/create-project.sh	project|dry-run|help|workflow-type|max-patch|max-minor|max-major|git-remote|priority|color|no-migrate|dev-tree|dev-tree-path|git-repo|git-repo-url|h	yes	non-idempotent	POST	/operations/create-project	CreateProjectBody	action	DualChannelShellEnvelope	module:pgai_agent_kanban.ops.projects.create_project
